<%# What a link preview (Discord, X, WhatsApp) reads of a shared card
    (CAP-9): its title and rarity, a fixed invitation line, in the URL's
    language, and never an image (no og:image, twitter:image or image_src:
    the game's art is not ours to show). The page stays out of search
    engines.
    - title: the card's title and rarity (shared_card_title);
    - url: the page's absolute, season-qualified URL, without query. %>
<% description = t("public_profiles.card.og_description") %>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<%= tag.meta name: "description", content: description %>
<%= tag.link rel: "canonical", href: url %>
<%= tag.meta property: "og:type", content: "website" %>
<%= tag.meta property: "og:site_name", content: t("layouts.application.application_name") %>
<%= tag.meta property: "og:title", content: title %>
<%= tag.meta property: "og:description", content: description %>
<%= tag.meta property: "og:url", content: url %>
<%= tag.meta property: "og:locale", content: og_locale %>
<%= tag.meta name: "twitter:card", content: "summary" %>
